    {
      "id": "hBES0U9M8guxOjCAYNKaj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1020,
      "y": 34940,
      "width": 1405.800048828125,
      "height": 495,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "fa3SMjfmhu5DlMwxbBKvQ",
        "zTDUk-yRTeC1dAoD6iZ5_",
        "fiLa55835S3NLU4ENgltO",
        "B_iGENWfubsF8PL-vL_hA",
        "NyA97lOdBg6qXf6_ACWaD"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c03r",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1357295069,
      "version": 382,
      "versionNonce": 1165521693,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793532368291,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n==> The OS solves this by breaking down RAM into fixed\n    4KB pages, allocating  on demand  and using a page table to map \n    from logical addresses to physical addresses\n\n==> The program sees a contiguous address space\n    but the OS can scatter those pages anywhere in physical memory\n\n==> The key insight is that nothing requires contiguous physical memory\n    Pages can be anywhere \n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n==> The OS solves this by breaking down RAM into fixed\n    4KB pages, allocating  on demand  and using a page table to map \n    from logical addresses to physical addresses\n\n==> The program sees a contiguous address space\n    but the OS can scatter those pages anywhere in physical memory\n\n==> The key insight is that nothing requires contiguous physical memory\n    Pages can be anywhere \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": 1793532362015,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
